    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d678">

                <pb facs="0863" n="751" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg751"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr. Hirsch</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-05-25"><hi rendition="#italic">May 25,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 217.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am gratified to learn by your No. 284 of
                    7th instant, that your note of 15th December last to the Porte, has apparently
                    had the effect to cause the unconditional issue to the Rev. Henry Easson of
                    Latakia, of the building permit which he had asked in vain of the local
                    authorities.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
